## Negative findings (why this file is `.excluded`)

**ZERO verified public benchmark numbers were found for this exact model/ID.** Per the self-exclusion rule this file is saved as `GLM_5.3.md.excluded` — no scored `.md` is written, and no placeholder scores are invented.

What was verified (platform/catalog metadata only, no measured numbers):

- **Identity:** MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview — a coding- and agent-focused preview model MiniMax quietly added to MiniMax Code (model picker alongside MiniMax-M3, M2.7, M2.7-highspeed) and the Token Plan on 2026-09-27. No announcement, model card, or technical report accompanied it.
- **Specs (confirmed from shipped configuration, per news fact-checks):** 1M-token context (a 512K configuration also ships), 128K max output; text/image/video in, text out; five reasoning-effort levels (low → max, default max); thinking cannot be turned off.
- **Positioning:** everyday coding work that benefits from lower latency (bug fixes, reviews, small features) rather than long reasoning runs.
- **Pricing:** none published — MiniMax Code / Token Plan subscription only; no public per-token price.
- **Suspected lineage (unconfirmed):** community fingerprinting has linked the free OpenRouter stealth model Space Bunny Alpha (see `model/space-bunny-alpha/`) to the same system days before this launch — MiniMax has not confirmed it.

Sources checked with no benchmark rows for this ID (2026-09-28):

- BenchLM (`minimax-m3-1-flash-preview`): page exists but **0 of 486 benchmarks covered** — "no source-displayable benchmark rows yet".
- Artificial Analysis: no page. BenchmarkList: no page. LLMReference: no page.
- MiniMax official channels: no model card, no benchmark report, no pricing page for the preview.
- News consensus (startupfortune, SaaSCity, AlphaSignal, DataNorth, hokai, eesel, ai-on-mac — 2026-09-27/28): all state no benchmarks were published with the release. A single low-authority content-farm article claims "73.8% SWE-bench Verified at 165 tok/s, $0.10/M input" — unconfirmed by MiniMax, absent from every benchmark tracker, and contradicted by the rest of the coverage; deliberately not treated as verified.

Interpolation from verified siblings (MiniMax-M3 = 54.78 BenchLM composite, M2.7 SWE-Pro 56.22%) was deliberately NOT used to fabricate dimension scores — those are different checkpoints. A future re-research should look for (a) a MiniMax model card or benchmark post once the preview graduates, (b) aggregator coverage (AA/BenchLM rows), or (c) published per-token pricing — then write a fresh `GLM_5.3.md`.

Scores inside this file are intentionally omitted/ignored: the sync skips `.excluded` files loudly.

